WEBVTT

1
00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:36.291


2
00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:39.000
<b>In the third chapter, Lord Krishna explained</b>

3
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.208
<b>how desire clouds our intellect,</b>

4
00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:47.916
<b>and simultaneously revealed, while practicing </b>
<b>selfless action (Nishkama Karma Yoga),</b>

5
00:00:47.916 --> 00:00:50.916
<b>how we can develop our spiritual knowledge,</b>

6
00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:55.750
<b>which helps liberate us from these desires.</b>

7
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:59.666
<b>Now in this fourth chapter, Krishna explains</b>

8
00:00:59.666 --> 00:01:05.875
<b>how we can attain this spiritual </b>
<b>knowledge and its benefits.</b>

9
00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:11.291
<b>The first step is to understand the </b>
<b>source of this spiritual knowledge</b>

10
00:01:11.291 --> 00:01:17.041
<b>and how it has been passed</b>
<b>down through human history.</b>

11
00:01:17.041 --> 00:01:22.416
<b>The opening verses of the fourth </b>
<b>chapter address precisely this.</b>

12
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.041
<b>Any disciple might naturally question</b>

13
00:01:30.041 --> 00:01:35.416
<b>whether the knowledge</b>
<b>they're receiving is authentic.</b>

14
00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:37.750
<b>Krishna, being omniscient,</b>

15
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:42.625
<b>anticipates that such a doubt </b>
<b>might arise in Arjuna's mind.</b>

16
00:01:42.625 --> 00:01:43.666
<b>Thus,</b>

17
00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:45.166
<b>in this first verse,</b>

18
00:01:45.166 --> 00:01:48.916
<b>He establishes the authenticity</b>
<b>of this spiritual knowledge,</b>

19
00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:51.375
<b>ensuring Arjuna understands</b>

20
00:01:51.375 --> 00:01:55.125
<b>that this wisdom isn't merely meant </b>
<b>to motivate him for battle,</b>

21
00:01:55.125 --> 00:02:00.541
<b>but rather is an eternal truth that has </b>
<b>existed for countless centuries.</b>

22
00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:02.000
<b>Krishna reveals that</b>

23
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.250
<b>He first shared this knowledge </b>
<b>with Vivasvan, the Sun God.</b>

24
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:12.625
<b>If you’ve noticed, it was mentioned</b>
<b>in previous chapters,</b>

25
00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:20.041
<b>just as earthly kingdoms have </b>
<b>various departments with their heads,</b>

26
00:02:20.041 --> 00:02:24.458
<b>the universe too has different departments</b>

27
00:02:24.458 --> 00:02:25.416
<b>- light,</b>

28
00:02:25.416 --> 00:02:26.416
<b>water,</b>

29
00:02:26.416 --> 00:02:28.041
<b>fire, and so forth –</b>

30
00:02:28.041 --> 00:02:32.250
<b>Each of these overseen by their specific deities.</b>

31
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:37.208
<b>Understand that the Sun isn't merely </b>
<b>a lifeless sphere radiating light –</b>

32
00:02:37.208 --> 00:02:40.083
<b>rather, behind it stands the Sun God, Vivasvan,</b>

33
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:47.708
<b>ensuring we continuously </b>
<b>receive light and energy. </b>

34
00:02:47.708 --> 00:02:51.625
<b>While Vivasvan isn't an earthly being,</b>

35
00:02:51.625 --> 00:02:59.458
<b>for simplicity, you can envision him as the divine</b>
<b>administrator of the energy department.</b>

36
00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:04.500
<b>But why did Krishna choose the Sun God as </b>
<b>the first recipient of this knowledge?</b>

37
00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:09.000
<b>Without light, can anyone see clearly?</b>

38
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.083
<b>The Sun God's very purpose is</b>

39
00:03:11.083 --> 00:03:13.750
<b>to dispel darkness.</b>

40
00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.458
<b>And this isn't just about physical darkness –</b>

41
00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:22.125
<b>it's about dispersing spiritual</b>
<b>darkness from our world.</b>

42
00:03:22.125 --> 00:03:26.375
<b>Who better than the Sun God to </b>
<b>undertake this mission?</b>

43
00:03:26.375 --> 00:03:30.083
<b>After receiving this spiritual wisdom from Krishna,</b>

44
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:33.375
<b>Sun God Vivasvan passed it to Manu,</b>

45
00:03:33.375 --> 00:03:38.833
<b>through whom this knowledge began </b>
<b>spreading throughout humanity.</b>

46
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:40.125
<b>We are all humans,</b>

47
00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:43.666
<b>and the word 'human' itself derives from Manu.</b>

48
00:03:43.666 --> 00:03:45.666
<b>The children of Manu,</b>

49
00:03:45.666 --> 00:03:46.833
<b>his descendants -</b>

50
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:50.000
<b>that's what we humans are, </b>
<b>all of us.</b>

51
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.166
<b>Subsequently,</b>

52
00:03:51.166 --> 00:03:55.291
<b>Manu transmitted this knowledge </b>
<b>to King Ikshvaku of his lineage,</b>

53
00:03:55.291 --> 00:04:00.333
<b>and it was in this Solar Dynasty that </b>
<b>Lord Rama would later be born.</b>

54
00:04:00.333 --> 00:04:07.625
<b>This illustrates how the Gita's wisdom has </b>
<b>existed in human society for millions of years.</b>

55
00:04:07.625 --> 00:04:08.625
<b>Now,</b>

56
00:04:08.625 --> 00:04:10.916
<b>when the need has arisen again,</b>

57
00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:13.625
<b>Krishna himself has taken human form,</b>

58
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:19.750
<b>standing on this battlefield of Mahabharata, </b>
<b>reviving this knowledge</b>

59
00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.833
<b>for the future generations to receive it.</b>

60
00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:24.750
<b>And yes,</b>

61
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:25.875
<b>remember,</b>

62
00:04:25.875 --> 00:04:29.541
<b>this knowledge was given to King Ikshvaku</b>

63
00:04:29.541 --> 00:04:34.916
<b>for a king's duty extends beyond merely</b>
<b>protecting his subjects' physical well-being –</b>

64
00:04:34.916 --> 00:04:37.625
<b>it includes safeguarding </b>
<b>their spiritual welfare as well.</b>

65
00:04:37.625 --> 00:04:40.291
<b>While we may no longer live in an age of kings,</b>

66
00:04:40.291 --> 00:04:47.000
<b>this responsibility now falls to </b>
<b>anyone in a position of leadership – </b>

67
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:55.333
<b>whether in family, society, or business.</b>

68
00:04:55.333 --> 00:04:59.750
<b>And now, this eternal knowledge, </b>
<b>this spiritual truth,</b>

69
00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.708
<b>stands before you through the Gita.</b>

70
00:05:01.708 --> 00:05:07.250
<b>Use it for your spiritual protection </b>
<b>and that of others.</b>

71
00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.625
<b>The knowledge of the Gita</b>

72
00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:18.208
<b>has the power to benefit all of humanity.</b>

73
00:05:18.208 --> 00:05:29.833
<b>This wisdom had to reach people across </b>
<b>different ages through various means.</b>

74
00:05:29.833 --> 00:05:33.708
<b>Now, think about this in reverse –</b>

75
00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:40.416
<b>can knowledge that's never shared </b>
<b>even be called knowledge?</b>

76
00:05:40.416 --> 00:05:43.958
<b>Or would you call it selfishness?</b>

77
00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:47.958
<b>Apply this to your personal life.</b>

78
00:05:47.958 --> 00:05:50.375
<b>Imagine</b>

79
00:05:50.375 --> 00:05:53.583
<b>you've developed a skill.</b>

80
00:05:53.583 --> 00:05:57.208
<b>Perhaps you're adept at cooking unique dishes</b>

81
00:05:57.208 --> 00:06:02.333
<b>or you've mastered a particular art form.</b>

82
00:06:02.333 --> 00:06:06.416
<b>Is this skill yours alone?</b>

83
00:06:06.416 --> 00:06:08.250
<b>No.</b>

84
00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:15.958
<b>You too learned this skill from </b>
<b>a well-wisher, a book, or a teacher.</b>

85
00:06:15.958 --> 00:06:22.041
<b>Then wouldn't it be inappropriate </b>
<b>to be selfish with it?</b>

86
00:06:22.041 --> 00:06:24.458
<b>Share it with others.</b>

87
00:06:24.458 --> 00:06:25.708
<b>Moreover,</b>

88
00:06:25.708 --> 00:06:31.000
<b>when you share your experiences </b>
<b>and knowledge with others,</b>

89
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:35.125
<b>not only do they benefit,</b>

90
00:06:35.125 --> 00:06:35.958
<b>but</b>

91
00:06:35.958 --> 00:06:41.791
<b>you also develop a sweet relationship with them,</b>

92
00:06:41.791 --> 00:06:45.541
<b>which brings even greater joy.</b>

93
00:06:45.541 --> 00:06:50.916
<b>And inspired by your selfless nature,</b>

94
00:06:50.916 --> 00:06:55.375
<b>they too will share their knowledge with others.</b>

95
00:06:55.375 --> 00:06:58.875
<b>This chain continues forward.</b>

96
00:06:58.875 --> 00:07:00.500
<b>Think</b>

97
00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.958
<b>how beautiful it is</b>

98
00:07:03.958 --> 00:07:10.875
<b>that your nature is indirectly</b>
<b>influencing so many lives.</b>

99
00:07:10.875 --> 00:07:15.083
<b>Additionally, this mutual relationship</b>

100
00:07:15.083 --> 00:07:18.291
<b>enhances your own knowledge.</b>

101
00:07:18.291 --> 00:07:23.750
<b>When you teach someone,</b>
<b>you gain a different perspective</b>

102
00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.500
<b>that helps you learn something new.</b>

103
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.625
<b>Consider it this way –</b>

104
00:07:29.625 --> 00:07:38.875
<b>by sharing your knowledge, you're planting</b>
<b>a seed that will grow into a mighty tree,</b>

105
00:07:38.875 --> 00:07:46.166
<b>whose fruits will be enjoyed by you </b>
<b>and many others for years to come.</b>

106
00:07:46.166 --> 00:07:50.083
<b>Just as sunlight nourishes plants,</b>

107
00:07:50.083 --> 00:07:54.583
<b>sharing knowledge nourishes the soul.</b>

108
00:07:54.583 --> 00:08:02.500
<b>When we teach others, we often</b>
<b>understand our subject better.</b>

109
00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:07.833
<b>Whether it's mutual cooperation, someone</b>
<b>else's welfare, or finding joy in it –</b>

110
00:08:07.833 --> 00:08:10.541
<b>the field doesn't matter.</b>

111
00:08:10.541 --> 00:08:18.541
<b>Consider how you're taking a significant </b>
<b>step toward spiritual progress as well.</b>

112
00:08:23.458 --> 00:08:26.208
<b>In this entire Bhagavad Gita,</b>

113
00:08:26.208 --> 00:08:33.166
<b>every verse's proper pronunciation, </b>
<b>translation, detailed description,</b>

114
00:08:33.166 --> 00:08:37.083
<b>and related lessons are provided</b>

115
00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:42.083
<b>so that you not only read this knowledge</b>

116
00:08:42.083 --> 00:08:43.916
<b>but understand it</b>

117
00:08:43.916 --> 00:08:48.666
<b>and ultimately implement it in your life.</b>

118
00:08:48.666 --> 00:08:54.125
<b>Knowledge isn't limited to</b>
<b>just reading or speaking –</b>

119
00:08:54.125 --> 00:08:59.750
<b>its true value lies in </b>
<b>understanding and explaining it.</b>

120
00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:04.958
<b>Now, take an example of a family environment.</b>

121
00:09:04.958 --> 00:09:14.583
<b>Consider a typical family where traditional </b>
<b>customs and religious rituals are observed.</b>

122
00:09:14.583 --> 00:09:20.000
<b>Often, these traditions are </b>
<b>passed down to the new generation</b>

123
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.333
<b>simply to be followed and carried forward.</b>

124
00:09:24.333 --> 00:09:25.375
<b>However,</b>

125
00:09:25.375 --> 00:09:27.666
<b>it's often seen</b>

126
00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:33.875
<b>that the new generation gradually </b>
<b>finds these traditions irrelevant,</b>

127
00:09:33.875 --> 00:09:37.041
<b>loses interest in them,</b>

128
00:09:37.041 --> 00:09:42.625
<b>and sometimes even opposes these customs.</b>

129
00:09:42.625 --> 00:09:45.041
<b>This is natural</b>

130
00:09:45.041 --> 00:09:52.125
<b>because often, these customs are handed </b>
<b>down without explaining their significance</b>

131
00:09:52.125 --> 00:09:55.750
<b>or the reasoning behind them.</b>

132
00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:58.708
<b>To bridge this gap, it's essential</b>

133
00:09:58.708 --> 00:10:03.875
<b>that family elders not only direct </b>
<b>the observance of traditions</b>

134
00:10:03.875 --> 00:10:12.000
<b>but also teach their history, logic behind them,</b>

135
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:15.458
<b>and most importantly,</b>

136
00:10:15.458 --> 00:10:19.833
<b>their relevance in today's times.</b>

137
00:10:19.833 --> 00:10:28.416
<b>And to accomplish this, family elders must </b>
<b>first master these subjects themselves.</b>

138
00:10:28.416 --> 00:10:35.208
<b>They need to study their spiritual, </b>
<b>cultural, and religious heritage.</b>

139
00:10:35.208 --> 00:10:40.625
<b>Practically, this can begin as a discussion.</b>

140
00:10:40.625 --> 00:10:43.166
<b>Take this very Gita as an example.</b>

141
00:10:43.166 --> 00:10:49.208
<b>You're studying it yourself, understanding</b>
<b>its descriptions and lessons.</b>

142
00:10:49.208 --> 00:10:52.833
<b>Now, if you make it a daily practice</b>

143
00:10:52.833 --> 00:10:55.708
<b>with the younger family members, </b>
<b>to share one verse, </b>

144
00:10:55.708 --> 00:11:02.166
<b>its meaning, context, and related teachings </b>
<b>to them.</b>

145
00:11:02.166 --> 00:11:05.958
<b>Imagine how beautiful that </b>
<b>environment would be.</b>

146
00:11:05.958 --> 00:11:10.500
<b>Whether it's the Gita or any </b>
<b>other tradition or knowledge,</b>

147
00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:15.083
<b>if taught to the new </b>
<b>generation in an engaging way,</b>

148
00:11:15.083 --> 00:11:19.958
<b>they will surely respect it in </b>
<b>the best possible manner.</b>

149
00:11:19.958 --> 00:11:23.541
<b>Additionally, throughout this process,</b>

150
00:11:23.541 --> 00:11:25.916
<b>in these mutual discussions,</b>

151
00:11:25.916 --> 00:11:29.583
<b>the entire family spends time together.</b>

152
00:11:29.583 --> 00:11:32.541
<b>This naturally increases family bonding.</b>

153
00:11:32.541 --> 00:11:35.916
<b>The family tree grows stronger.</b>

154
00:11:35.916 --> 00:11:37.791
<b>Think about it.</b>

155
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:46.666
<b>For the efficient leadership </b>
<b>of this universe, it's essential</b>

156
00:11:46.666 --> 00:11:53.458
<b>that I distribute this knowledge of the </b>
<b>Gita in every age, every generation.</b>

157
00:11:53.458 --> 00:11:57.333
<b>Only then will humanity benefit from it,</b>

158
00:11:57.333 --> 00:12:02.708
<b>only then will the earthly realm continue </b>
<b>to function in an organized manner.</b>

159
00:12:02.708 --> 00:12:05.750
<b>On a smaller scale,</b>

160
00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:12.791
<b>your organization and you </b>
<b>yourself can learn from this.</b>

161
00:12:12.791 --> 00:12:17.541
<b>If you're in a leadership position, it's essential</b>

162
00:12:17.541 --> 00:12:22.791
<b>that the organization's culture, systems, </b>
<b>and proper procedures</b>

163
00:12:22.791 --> 00:12:29.291
<b>not only reach your colleagues working </b>
<b>under you</b>

164
00:12:29.291 --> 00:12:30.125
<b>but</b>

165
00:12:30.125 --> 00:12:37.666
<b>that they understand them, follow them, </b>
<b>and also transmit them to others.</b>

166
00:12:37.666 --> 00:12:44.375
<b>This is necessary because new people </b>
<b>constantly join every organization.</b>

167
00:12:44.375 --> 00:12:49.500
<b>If they don't understand the culture, </b>
<b>not only will they struggle,</b>

168
00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:54.458
<b>but it will also adversely affect </b>
<b>the organization's objectives.</b>

169
00:12:54.458 --> 00:12:56.166
<b>In the professional world,</b>

170
00:12:56.166 --> 00:12:58.625
<b>senior officials' duty</b>

171
00:12:58.625 --> 00:13:01.458
<b>isn't just to give instructions or orders,</b>

172
00:13:01.458 --> 00:13:07.125
<b>but to see themselves as guides.</b>

173
00:13:07.125 --> 00:13:12.583
<b>Such guides who bear the responsibility </b>
<b>of training young employees</b>

174
00:13:12.583 --> 00:13:18.791
<b>and preparing them for </b>
<b>organizational responsibilities.</b>

175
00:13:18.791 --> 00:13:22.166
<b>This can be done in various ways –</b>

176
00:13:22.166 --> 00:13:26.875
<b>by involving young members</b>
<b>in important projects,</b>

177
00:13:26.875 --> 00:13:30.041
<b>making them part of the </b>
<b>decision-making process,</b>

178
00:13:30.041 --> 00:13:33.166
<b>teaching them when mistakes occur.</b>

179
00:13:33.166 --> 00:13:34.500
<b>Moreover,</b>

180
00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.791
<b>it's essential for senior officials</b>

181
00:13:37.791 --> 00:13:42.333
<b>to occasionally take on a supporting role,</b>

182
00:13:42.333 --> 00:13:49.541
<b>giving leadership reins to others, </b>
<b>so they too can learn to face challenges.</b>

183
00:13:49.541 --> 00:13:53.833
<b>The true mark of leadership isn't just control –</b>

184
00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:57.666
<b>The true mark of leadership is,</b>

185
00:13:57.666 --> 00:14:04.541
<b>identifying other capable individuals </b>
<b>like yourself and training them.</b>

186
00:14:04.541 --> 00:14:09.416
<b>And encouraging such a culture in the organization.</b>

187
00:14:09.416 --> 00:14:11.291
<b>Think about it.</b>

188
00:14:11.291 --> 00:14:14.458
<b>Are you controlling?</b>

189
00:14:14.458 --> 00:14:16.208
<b>Or leading?</b>

